.TH XYMON-PLUGIN 8 "November 21, 2026" "xymon-plugins"
.SH NAME
xymon-plugin \- install, update and check the Xymon plugins, itself among them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "xymon-plugin install|update|enable|disable|remove|status|verify|outdated|clean [--server|--tools] [--all] [PLUGIN...] [NAME=value...]"
.br
.B "xymon-plugin --version"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xymon-plugin
installs each plugin of the xymon-plugins repository from its
.I PLUGIN
file: on a Xymon server under
.IR $XYMONHOME/ext/NAME/ ,
elsewhere under
.IR $PREFIX/libexec/xymon-plugins/NAME/ .
It is run from a checkout or a release's archive as
.BR ./xymon-plugin ,
a link to
.IR plugins/xymon-plugin/xymon-plugin .
.PP
It is a plugin itself:
.B "./xymon-plugin install --server xymon-plugin"
installs it into
.I $XYMONHOME/ext/xymon-plugin/
with its
.IR PLUGIN ,
.I VERSION
and
.I MANIFEST
files, so that
.B status
and
.B outdated
report its own version beside the others'. The copy installed gives its
version, and runs
.BR status ,
.B verify
and
.B outdated
on what is installed; it holds no plugin, so
.B status
says of each that it is not in this copy. To install or update plugins,
run the checkout's or the archive's.
.PP
Every verb and setting is described in the repository's
.I README.md
and
.IR plugins/README.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
The installer's version: its
.I PLUGIN
file's, beside it when installed, under
.I plugins/xymon-plugin/
in a checkout or an archive.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error, 2 for a usage error;
.B verify
ends with 3 when something is broken and 4 when it is only untidy,
.B outdated
with 7 when a plugin's
.I VERSION
cannot be compared, else 6 when a newer release exists, as
.I plugins/README.md
says.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XYMONHOME/ext/xymon-plugin/
The installer, installed on a server.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xymonapi (8)
